+## Full filtered and integral relative upgrade
 
-LM2 E.4 correctly observes that the absolute unipotent completion of C2*C3 is trivial. Retaining S3 corrects that problem, but also changes the source radical from rank two to rank seven. B.25 makes that correction explicit, and B.26–B.27 solve the resulting existential associated-graded compatibility problem. Thus q7 passes this particular test even though its pentagon defect is nonzero by B.12.
+B.30 works with the actual relative groups and quotient maps. A finite Levi splitting gives a genuine deck action on the rank-seven radical and, by taking its image, on the rank-two target. The quotient by actual deck commutators is the absolute completion of F2 by its universal property. Filling kills the five stated peripheral classes. An invariant outer action can be made strictly deck-centralizing because finite-group H1 on a prounipotent group over Q vanishes by successive averaging. Its two descendants are peripheral; for the covering map this uses unique square and cube roots.
+
